// Generated by website/sync-docs.mjs from docs/. Do not edit by hand.
window.RENDRIX_DOCS = {
  "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md": "# Architecture\r\n\r\nRendrix is a rendering engine and application runtime. TypeScript applications run inside it and are\r\ndrawn by its own GPU pipeline: there is no Chromium, Electron, WebView or system browser involved,\r\nand Rendrix makes no attempt to be API-compatible with any of them.\r\n\r\n```\r\n your TypeScript / TSX            rendrix CLI (Node)                       rendrix-runtime (Rust)\r\n ───────────────────  build ───▶  type-check, transpile to ES modules ──▶  ┌──────────────────────────────┐\r\n index.html, styles.css           pack  .rdxapp  (JSON bundle)             │ rendrix-js   QuickJS + Web APIs│\r\n                                  or  standalone executable                │ rendrix-core DOM → style →     │\r\n                                                                           │              boxes → layout →  │\r\n        OS input ◀──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │              display list      │\r\n        (winit)  ──▶ Session ──▶ DOM events ──▶ your handlers ──▶ DOM ───▶ │ rendrix-gfx  wgpu renderer    │\r\n                                                                           └──────────────────────────────┘\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Crates (`engine/crates/`)\r\n\r\n| Crate | Responsibility | Interface other crates rely on |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| `rendrix-css` | Tokenizer/parser, selectors + specificity, cascade, inheritance, custom properties (`var()`), media queries, `@keyframes`, timing functions, interpolation, computed style | `SelectorElement` trait (style any tree), `ComputedStyle`, `compute_style` |\r\n| `rendrix-dom` | Arena DOM: nodes, attributes, mutation records, selector queries, tolerant HTML parser/serializer, form state, dirty tracking, node GC | `Document`; `ElRef` implements `SelectorElement` |\r\n| `rendrix-layout` | Layout-engine-neutral box tree and the `LayoutEngine` trait; a persistent Taffy backend (flex, grid, block) that only re-lays out what changed | `LayoutNode`, `LayoutEngine`, `TextMeasurer` |\r\n| `rendrix-gfx` | Display list, cosmic-text shaping + paragraph cache + disk font-DB cache, glyph atlas with LRU, wgpu renderer (SDF rounded rects/per-side/dashed borders/gradients/shadows/clips/transforms, images, text), a shared atlas that batches small images into one draw, offscreen compositing layers (isolated opacity, separable Gaussian blur, real backdrop-filter), CPU-rasterized Canvas 2D, SVG painting and 3D scene rasterization with dynamic uniform offsets | `DisplayList`, `TextSystem`, `Renderer`, `Canvas` |\r\n| `rendrix-core` | `Engine`: DOM → styles (+transitions/animations) → incremental box generation and dirty-subtree patching (block/inline/flex/grid, anonymous boxes, whitespace, replaced elements, form controls) → layout → painting; hit testing, scrolling, text editing | `Engine::update(now)`, `hit_test`, `edit`, `display_list` |\r\n| `rendrix-js` | `JsEngine` trait + QuickJS backend, ES module loader, DOM and Web API prelude (JavaScript), host operations, event-loop glue, dedicated workers, source-map remapping and the AccessKit tree builder | `JsEngine`, `Host`, `JsRuntime` |\r\n| `rendrix-runtime` | App bundle loader, `Session` (input state machine and frame loop), winit window driver (multi-window, touch, gamepads, IME), headless driver, benchmark, `--inspect` snapshot | `Session`, `AppBundle` |\r\n| `rendrix-web` | Experimental wasm32 target: the same engine running in a Web Worker with the browser's JS engine and a transferred `OffscreenCanvas` | `WebApp`, `BrowserEngine` |\r\n\r\n## One frame\r\n\r\n1. **Platform events** (winit) are translated by the window driver into `Session` calls: `pointer_move`,\r\n   `pointer_down`, `key_down`, `wheel`, `text_commit`, `resize`.\r\n2. `Session` hit-tests against the previous frame's geometry and dispatches **real DOM events**\r\n   (`pointerover/enter/move/down/up`, `mouse*`, `click`, `keydown`, `input`, `change`, `focus*`, `wheel`…)\r\n   through the JavaScript event system with capture → target → bubble phases. Default actions run only if\r\n   no handler called `preventDefault()`: focus, click activation (checkbox, radio, label, form submit),\r\n   caret placement and drag-selection, Tab traversal, text editing, scrolling.\r\n3. Timers, completed fetches and microtasks run; then `requestAnimationFrame` callbacks.\r\n4. `Engine::update(now)`:\r\n   - rebuild stylesheets if `<style>`/`<link>` or the media context changed;\r\n   - **restyle** only what changed: dirty subtrees for attribute/class/inline-style changes; for\r\n     hover/active/focus and child-list changes only the element itself, descending when the computed style\r\n     changed or the stylesheet has non-local state/structural selectors;\r\n   - if no computed style actually changed (most hovers), the frame stops here;\r\n   - start transitions/keyframe animations from style changes and sample running ones;\r\n   - patch the **box tree** per element for dirty subtrees instead of rebuilding it (formatting-context\r\n     rules, anonymous boxes) and run layout (Taffy keeps its tree between frames, so unchanged subtrees\r\n     reuse cached results);\r\n   - paint to a **display list** with stacking order, clips, transforms and viewport culling, producing\r\n     the hit-test list in the same traversal. Pixel-reading effects (`filter: blur()`, `backdrop-filter`,\r\n     polygon clips) route through isolated offscreen compositing layers; ordinary frames keep the\r\n     single-draw-call path.\r\n5. `Renderer` flattens the display list into one instance buffer and draws it in a single pipeline and\r\n   usually one draw call. Canvas content is uploaded as its own texture and composited in the same pass.\r\n\r\nAn idle application does no work: no timer, no animation and no pending change means no frame.\r\n\r\n## Replaceable parts\r\n\r\n* **JavaScript engine.** Only `quickjs.rs` names `rquickjs`. The rest of the runtime talks to a `JsEngine`\r\n  trait (eval script/module, call a global, drain jobs) and exposes native functionality through a single\r\n  entry point, `__native(op, ...args)`, implemented by `Host`. The Web API surface is JavaScript\r\n  (`prelude/*.js`) built on those operations, so another engine needs the trait implementation and the same\r\n  entry point.\r\n* **Layout engine.** Layout consumes `LayoutNode` + `ComputedStyle`, never DOM types. Taffy is one\r\n  implementation of `LayoutEngine`.\r\n* **Text.** Layout measures through `TextMeasurer`; only `rendrix-gfx` shapes text.\r\n\r\n## Modules and TypeScript\r\n\r\nThe runtime never sees TypeScript. `rendrix build` type-checks with the project's `tsconfig.json`, transpiles\r\nevery module to ES2022 with the TypeScript compiler API, resolves bare specifiers from `node_modules`\r\n(ESM only), rewrites imports to bundle paths and emits a `rendrix-app/1` JSON bundle. QuickJS loads the\r\nmodules natively (static imports, `import()`, top-level `await`). JSX compiles to\r\n`rendrix/jsx-runtime`, which builds DOM nodes directly (no virtual DOM).\r\n\r\n## Memory model\r\n\r\nDOM nodes live in a Rust arena. JavaScript wrappers are weak handles registered with a\r\n`FinalizationRegistry`; wrappers of connected nodes are also held strongly so identity, expando properties\r\nand listeners survive GC. Listener state is keyed by node id, never stored on the wrapper. Detached subtrees\r\nwith no live wrapper are freed by a periodic sweep and their ids reused.\r\n\r\n## Known architectural limits\r\n\r\n* Box generation is incremental per dirty subtree, but Taffy still re-solves the affected layout tree\r\n  (≈5–7 ms for a mutation on 9,000 nodes). Getting mutations under 3 ms is the open performance step.\r\n* Overlay scrollbars are painted but not draggable. The AccessKit accessibility tree and OS bridge exist\r\n  ([ACCESSIBILITY_PLAN.md](ACCESSIBILITY_PLAN.md)), but no manual screen-reader pass has been recorded.\r\n* Absolutely positioned boxes use the containing block's origin when their insets are `auto` (no static\r\n  position), and inline elements with box styling (padding, background…) behave as inline-blocks.\r\n* Each window has its own `Session` and JavaScript context; windows do not share a document or clipboard\r\n  beyond the OS clipboard. There is one process and no isolation for hostile code.\r\n* Tables, floats and multi-column are laid out as grid-like approximations; CSS masks, 3D and the web\r\n  target are partial. See [COMPATIBILITY.md](COMPATIBILITY.md).\r\n\r\nSee [COMPATIBILITY.md](COMPATIBILITY.md) for exactly what is and is not supported, and\r\n[ROADMAP.md](ROADMAP.md) for current status. [ENGINE_ASSESSMENT.md](ENGINE_ASSESSMENT.md) is the dated\r\nassessment from the start of the engine rewrite.\r\n",
  "docs/COMPATIBILITY.md": "# Compatibility matrix\r\n\r\nRendrix is **not a browser** and does not claim browser compatibility. This page lists what is\r\nimplemented and covered by an automated test (✅), implemented with known gaps (🟡), and not\r\nimplemented (❌). Anything not listed is not supported. Tests live next to the code:\r\n`engine/crates/*/src` (unit), `engine/crates/rendrix-runtime/tests` (input/frame integration, GPU pixels),\r\n`packages/cli/test` (build pipeline, runs bundles in the real runtime).\r\n\r\nManually verified platform: **Windows 11, NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060, Vulkan** (windowed at 125 % DPI and\r\nheadless). macOS and Linux are built and tested in CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`), but no GPU-visible\r\nmanual run has been recorded there; GPU tests skip themselves when CI has no adapter. The same distinction\r\napplies to the non-x64 Windows and Linux packaging targets: compile-checked or cross-packaged, not manually\r\nrun on hardware here.\r\n\r\nArchitecture note: the verified Windows platform above is **x64**. Windows **ARM64** (`aarch64-pc-windows-msvc`,\r\nkey `win32-arm64`) and **x86 / 32-bit** (`i686-pc-windows-msvc` / `i686-pc-windows-gnu`, aliases `x86` / `ia32`,\r\nkey `win32-x86`) are supported packaging targets compile-checked in CI, but neither has been manually run on\r\nhardware here — treat them as packaged/compile-checked, not hardware-verified.\r\n\r\nThe same applies to the non-x64/arm64 Linux keys: `linux-x86` (`i686-unknown-linux-gnu`), `linux-armv7`\r\n(`armv7-unknown-linux-gnueabihf`, aliases `armv7` / `armhf`, the Raspberry Pi 32-bit target) and\r\n`linux-riscv64` (`riscv64gc-unknown-linux-gnu`, alias `riscv64`) are **packaging targets** — the CLI resolves\r\nand cross-packages them (target resolution is test-covered), and CI compile-checks the runtime for each\r\ntriple, but no Linux build of any architecture has been manually run with GPU-visible output here.\r\n\r\n## JavaScript and modules\r\n\r\n| Feature | Status | Notes |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| ES2023 language, classes, private fields, `async`/`await`, generators | ✅ | Provided by the pinned QuickJS-ng through `rquickjs 0.14`, including `BigInt`, `WeakRef`, `FinalizationRegistry`, `Object.groupBy`, `toSorted` and `Array.fromAsync`. The last three come from the vendored QuickJS-ng and are not separately covered by in-tree tests |\r\n| ES modules, relative imports, top-level `await` | ✅ | Bare specifiers resolved at build time (ESM packages only) |\r\n| Dynamic `import()` | ✅ | Provided by QuickJS; the build rewrites static and dynamic specifiers to bundle paths (variable specifiers pass through to the runtime loader). Covered by CLI rewrite tests and `rendrix-js` chunk/TLA ordering tests plus a `Session` end-to-end test |\r\n| CommonJS / `require` / Node built-ins | ❌ | Build error with an explanation |\r\n| TypeScript, TSX | ✅ | Same transpile/bundle path as JS; type-checked with project `tsconfig.json` (`allowJs: true`, `checkJs: false` default; `rendrix build/check --check-js` opts JS into checking). Directories with TS/JSX must go through `rendrix dev`/`build` — `AppBundle::from_directory` is dev-JS-only and errors actionably |\r\n| Source maps | ✅ | `tsc` maps stored per module in `bundle.sourceMaps` (`rendrix-app/1` unchanged — additive field); runtime remaps `at name (file:line:col)` frames, invalid maps ignored |\r\n| Promises, microtask order, `queueMicrotask`, unhandled-rejection events | ✅ | Runaway scripts are interrupted by an execution budget (default 5 s/task) and reported as errors |\r\n| `setTimeout`/`setInterval`/`requestAnimationFrame` | ✅ | Frame-driven rAF; timers on the platform clock |\r\n| `Intl`, `WebAssembly`, `Temporal` | ❌ | Not provided by the prelude or the pinned QuickJS build; `toLocaleString` works without locale data. Dedicated `Worker` is implemented and tested — see the Workers row below |\r\n\r\n## DOM\r\n\r\n| Feature | Status | Notes |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| Node, Element, Text, Comment, Document, DocumentFragment, tree mutation, errors as `DOMException` | ✅ | |\r\n| Attributes, `classList`, `dataset`, `style` (live), `innerHTML`/`outerHTML`, `insertAdjacent*`, `cloneNode` | ✅ | HTML parser is tolerant, not the full HTML5 tree builder (no foster parenting) |\r\n| `querySelector(All)`, `matches`, `closest`, `getElementsBy*` | ✅ | Type/class/id/attribute selectors, all combinators, `:not :is :where :nth-* :first/last-child :empty :root :hover :active :focus :focus-visible :disabled :checked`, `:has()` (descendant/child/sibling combinators). `:focus-visible` follows input modality (keyboard/a11y/programmatic focus shows it, pointer focus does not) |\r\n| Events: capture/target/bubble, `once`, `passive`, `signal`, `on*` properties, `stopImmediatePropagation`, `CustomEvent` | ✅ | |\r\n| Mouse/Pointer/Wheel/Keyboard/Input/Focus/Submit events from the OS | ✅ | Touch (tap/pan/fling/long-press/multi-touch, `touch-action`) and desktop gamepads (`gilrs`) are forwarded into the same `Session`; pointer capture is a no-op. Mobile OS shells (Android NDK / iOS) do not exist yet |\r\n| Form controls: `input` (text-like, checkbox, radio, button), `textarea`, `select`, `button`, `label`, `form` | 🟡 | Typing, caret, selection, clipboard, `input`/`change`, label and submit activation work. Undo/redo via Ctrl+Z/Y (50-entry per-control history). Full constraint validation (`validity`, `checkValidity`/`reportValidity`/`setCustomValidity`, `required`/`pattern`/`minlength`/`maxlength`/`min`/`max`/`step`, email/url/number types, `invalid` events; `reportValidity` focuses the first invalid control — no visual bubble UI). `select` has keyboard navigation (arrows/Home/End) and `showPicker()` (renders an in-engine popup list). `stepUp`/`stepDown`/`valueAsDate` work. `input[type=file].showPicker()` opens the real OS file dialog (populates `files` with `File` objects carrying `path`, bytes still read via `rendrix.fs` with permission); `input[type=date].showPicker()` opens an in-engine calendar. Popups are engine-rendered, not OS widgets |\r\n| `getBoundingClientRect`, `offset*`, `client*`, `scroll*`, `scrollIntoView`, `elementFromPoint`, `getComputedStyle` | 🟡 | `getComputedStyle` implements a fixed list of properties (display, position, colour, size, margin/padding/border, font, opacity, overflow, z-index, transform, filter, backdrop-filter, clip-path, mask-image, text-shadow, text-overflow, custom properties); others return `\"\"` |\r\n| `MutationObserver` | ✅ | childList, attributes (+filter, old value), characterData, subtree |\r\n| `ResizeObserver` | ✅ | `contentRect` plus `contentBoxSize`/`borderBoxSize`/`devicePixelContentBoxSize`; `observe(el, { box })` accepts `content-box`, `border-box` and `device-pixel-content-box`, with DPR scaling and invalid-value errors. Delivered per animation frame; covered by `rendrix-js` tests |\r\n| `IntersectionObserver`, Shadow DOM, custom elements, `Range`/`Selection`, `contenteditable`, drag and drop | ✅/🟡 | `IntersectionObserver` ✅ (thresholds, rootMargin). Shadow DOM ✅ minimal: `attachShadow({mode})` open/closed roots, `shadowRoot`, `customElements.define/get/whenDefined/upgrade` with `connectedCallback`/`disconnectedCallback` on insert/remove. `Range` ✅ (offsets, `selectNode/Contents`, `cloneRange`), `Selection` ✅ singleton (`addRange`/`getRangeAt`/`selectAllChildren`/`toString`). `contenteditable` ✅ reflection + `document.designMode` + `execCommand('insertText'/'delete'/'selectAll')`. Drag and drop 🟡: native OS file drops only (see row below) |\r\n\r\n## CSS\r\n\r\n| Feature | Status | Notes |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| Cascade: origin, specificity, `!important`, source order, inheritance, `inherit`/`initial`/`unset`, custom properties and `var()` with fallbacks | ✅ | |\r\n| Media queries (`width`, `height`, `orientation`, `prefers-color-scheme`, `resolution`, `and`/`not`/`,`) | ✅ | Re-evaluated on resize |\r\n| Box model, `box-sizing`, margin/padding/border, `border-radius` | ✅ | Per-side border colours and dashed/dotted styles render in the shader (`double` falls back to solid) |\r\n| `display`: block, inline, inline-block, flex, inline-flex, grid, table roles, list-item, none, contents | ✅/🟡 | Block/flex/grid/none/contents ✅. Table roles (`table`, `table-row`, `table-cell`, row groups, caption, columns) parse and collapse to a grid-like layout (🟡, see Tables row). `list-item` behaves as block; `<li>` keeps its marker run |\r\n| Flexbox (all properties) | ✅ | Taffy |\r\n| Grid (tracks, `repeat`, `minmax`, `fr`, auto-fill/fit, line and span placement, gaps) | ✅ | `grid-template-areas` and `grid-area` names implemented |\r\n| Positioning: relative, absolute, fixed, sticky, z-index and stacking order | 🟡 | `sticky` lays out at its static position and clamps inside the nearest scrollport at paint time (release within the containing block is not modelled); static position of auto-inset absolutes is the container origin |\r\n| Overflow: hidden/clip/scroll/auto, wheel scrolling, nested scrollers | ✅ | Scrollbars are overlay indicators, not draggable |\r\n| Tables (`display: table` / `table-row` / `table-cell`, row groups, `caption`) | 🟡 | Collapses to a grid-like layout: one `1fr` track per column (an explicit `grid-template-*` wins), rows and row groups dissolve, cells are grid items, `col`/`colgroup` generate no box. `colspan`/`rowspan`, automatic column sizing, anonymous table objects and missing-`tbody` insertion are ❌ |\r\n| Floats (`float: left` / `right`, `clear`) | 🟡 | Floated boxes pin to the content edge (explicit widths only; auto-width floats size like blocks) and stay in-flow; `clear` pushes the box (and everything after it) below preceding floats in the same block. No text wrap around floats, no side-by-side packing (floats stack vertically), containers do not auto-expand around floats, floats never interact across containing blocks |\r\n| Multi-column (`column-count`, `column-width`, `columns`, `column-span: all`) | 🟡 | The container becomes N equal `1fr` tracks (from `column-count`, or derived from `column-width` against the viewport width); children flow row-wise. No balancing, no `column-fill`, non-`all` spanners ignored, `column-rule` ❌ |\r\n| `writing-mode` | ❌ | |\r\n| Text: font family/size/weight/style, line-height, letter-spacing, alignment, decoration, transform, `white-space`, wrapping | ✅ | Shaping is cosmic-text (bidi/complex scripts are not covered by tests). `text-overflow: ellipsis` ✅ (nowrap, longest-`…`-fitting prefix via binary search, multi-run preserving); `word-break` (`normal`/`break-all`/`keep-all`) and `-webkit-line-clamp` ✅ (line-limited content rewrite with a trailing `…`); `text-shadow` renders as shadow-tinted text copies beneath the text (offset exact; blur softens through reduced alpha — a box-blur approximation) |\r\n| Colours (hex, `rgb`, `hsl`, named, alpha), gradients (linear/radial, ≤ 4 stops), `box-shadow` (outer + inset), `opacity`, `background-image: url()`, `object-fit` | 🟡 | Shadow blur is an analytic approximation. `opacity` on a subtree creates an isolated offscreen group, so overlapping translucent siblings blend with each other before compositing (nested opacity multiplies correctly). Small images (≤512 px per edge) pack into a shared atlas and batch into one draw; large images and canvases keep dedicated textures |\r\n| 2D `transform`, `transform-origin` | ✅ | No 3D, no `perspective` |\r\n| Transitions and `@keyframes` animations | ✅ | Animatable: opacity, colours, lengths, margin/padding, inset, transform, box-shadow, gap, flex-grow, font-size. Others switch discretely |\r\n| `calc()` | ✅ | Mixed units (`%` + px offsets, viewport units baked), `+ - * /`, parens and nesting; pure expressions fold to `Px`/`Percent` |\r\n| `@font-face` | 🟡 | Local bundled TTF/OTF/TTC only; WOFF/WOFF2 ❌ |\r\n| `::before`/`::after` with string `content` | ✅ | `attr()`, counters, images ❌ |\r\n| `filter`, `backdrop-filter`, `clip-path`, `mask` | 🟡 | Effects that read pixels run through an isolated offscreen compositing layer: `filter: blur()` is a separable two-pass Gaussian (~±3.5σ, 14 taps; brightness/grayscale stay exact pointwise), `backdrop-filter` really filters the painted backdrop (also with translucent page backgrounds, without double-compositing), and `clip-path: polygon()` clips per pixel. `inset()`/`circle()`/`ellipse()` clips remain exact. `mask-image: url()` still applies the mask's average alpha (spatially-varying masks remain approximated — the layer has a mask slot but paint does not fill it yet). All four establish a stacking context. Nesting (`&` + descendant + `@media`-in-rule scoping) ✅ and `@import` ✅ are implemented. `@supports` conditions are really evaluated against the property parser (`and`/`or`/`not()`, `selector()`); `@layer` ordering ✅ (normal order, reversed for `!important`); `@container` size queries ✅ against the nearest `container-type` ancestor's box (size map refreshed from layout, one extra frame to converge; `cqw`/`cqh` units ❌) |\r\n\r\n## Web platform APIs\r\n\r\n| API | Status | Notes |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| `URL`, `URLSearchParams` | ✅ | No IDNA/punycode |\r\n| `TextEncoder`, `TextDecoder` | ✅ | UTF-8, latin1/ascii |\r\n| `AbortController`/`AbortSignal` (`timeout`, `any`) | ✅ | |\r\n| `fetch`, `Headers`, `Request`, `Response`, `Blob`, `File`, `FormData` | 🟡 | Relative URLs read bundled assets; `data:` URLs; `http(s)` only when `permissions.network` is true. `FormData` encodes RFC 7578 multipart; a per-app session cookie jar persists cookies for the process lifetime with `Max-Age`/`Expires` expiry and a live `document.cookie` view (`navigator.cookieEnabled` is `true`). `document.cookie` is scoped to the `rendrix://app` origin, so it does not see cookies from HTTP fetch hosts. No streaming `ReadableStream` bodies (`Body.body` is `null`; use `text()`/`json()`/`arrayBuffer()`), no CORS/cache — documented native scope: Rendrix is a single-origin `rendrix://app` runtime, not a browser |\r\n| `WebSocket` | ✅ | `ws://`/`wss://` (rustls, native cert roots posture matching `ureq`), subprotocols, text/binary (binaryType `arraybuffer`/`blob`), `bufferedAmount`, close codes/reasons, `wss` needs `permissions.network` (loopback `ws://127.0.0.1` is always allowed for tests). Delivery is frame-budgeted (≤16 messages/frame, spill to next tick) and never blocks the frame loop |\r\n| `localStorage`, `sessionStorage` | ✅ | Local storage is a per-user JSON file keyed by app name; no `storage` events |\r\n| `crypto.getRandomValues`, `randomUUID`, `crypto.subtle.digest` | 🟡 | OS CSPRNG. `subtle.digest` supports SHA-1/256/384/512 and accepts `ArrayBuffer`/views; other `SubtleCrypto` methods (`importKey`, `sign`, `encrypt`, …) ❌ |\r\n| `structuredClone`, `atob`/`btoa`, `performance.now`, `matchMedia`, `console` | ✅ | |\r\n| `navigator.clipboard` | 🟡 | Text only; fed by Copy/Cut in text controls |\r\n| Images via `<img>`, CSS backgrounds, `new Image()` with `load`/`error` | 🟡 | PNG is tested. JPEG, GIF (first frame) and WebP go through the same `image`-crate decoder but have no tests. SVG (`.svg` files, inline `<svg>`, and SVG `drawImage` sources): `rect`/`circle`/`ellipse`/`line`/`polyline`/`polygon`/`path` (M/L/H/V/C/S/Q/T/Z) with solid fills and strokes, CPU-rasterized with no new dependencies (hand-rolled, mirrors the Canvas2D raster conventions); `<text>`, gradients, filters, masks, percentage lengths, external refs ❌. No animation |\r\n| `location`, `history` | 🟡 | In-memory; there is no navigation |\r\n| Canvas 2D | ✅ (subset) | `getContext('2d')` returns a full CPU-rasterized context composited as a GPU texture: paths/fill (`nonzero`/`evenodd`)/stroke, transforms, linear/radial/conic gradients, `Path2D` (own path object for `fill`/`stroke`/`clip`; no SVG-string constructor), `clip()` (intersecting, restored on `save`/`restore`), `fillText`/`strokeText`/`measureText` with `font`/`textAlign`/`textBaseline` (shaped through the shared `TextSystem`; glyphs stay axis-aligned under rotation/skew), shadows (`shadowColor`/`Blur`/`OffsetX`/`OffsetY`, box-blur approximation; `drawImage` casts no shadow), `drawImage`, `get/putImageData`, `toDataURL`, `toBlob` (PNG), and `globalCompositeOperation` (Porter-Duff modes plus separable blends; non-separable hue/saturation/color/luminosity fall back to source-over). `OffscreenCanvas` ✅ (backed by a detached canvas, `convertToBlob`/`transferToImageBitmap`); video sources, patterns, filters and `webgpu`/`bitmaprenderer` (null) remain ❌. Canvas draws mark only the canvas element dirty |\r\n| Canvas 3D (WebGL subset + `RendrixScene`) | 🟡 (subset) | One JS desc API, **two rendering paths**. `RendrixScene.createScene(canvas, desc)` / `setCamera` / `addBox` / `addPlane` / `update` / `remove` (+ `Rendrix3D.createBoxScene`); alias `canvas.getContext('webgl'|'webgl2')` supports `clearColor`/`clear`/`enable(DEPTH_TEST)`/`viewport`, `createBuffer`/`bindBuffer`/`bufferData`, `drawArrays(TRIANGLES)` and a `{position,color}` uniform path. **Plain `<canvas>`**: CPU-rasterized into the bitmap (flat Lambert + ambient, painter's algorithm, no depth buffer or clipping). **`<rendrix-scene>` / `<canvas data-3d>`**: GPU wgpu forward pass (`scene3d.wgsl`) with Depth24Plus testing, indexed meshes, frustum culling, Blinn-Phong with up to 4 directional + 4 point lights (optional range falloff) plus summed ambient, `material.color[3] < 1` alpha blending with back-to-front sorting, `material.cull: \"none\"|\"back\"|\"front\"`, and per-scene/per-mesh dynamic uniform slots (multiple scenes per frame). Desc: `camera{ fovY,near,far,position,lookAt }`, `meshes[{ geo{ kind:\"box\"|\"plane\"|\"sphere\"|\"tris\",size|verts|uvs }, material{ color,metal,rough,emissive,cull,textureId }, transform{ pos,rotEulerDeg,scale } }]`, `lights[{ kind:\"dir\"|\"ambient\"|\"point\",dir|pos,color,intensity,range }]`, `background`. `RendrixScene.setTexture(id, rgba, w, h)` stages an RGBA texture for `material.textureId`; procedural primitives have 0..1 UVs, `tris` accepts explicit `geo.uvs` or falls back to a planar X/Y projection. A scene-owned canvas repaints fully per upload; empty transparent scenes are a no-op; scenes die with their element. Still ❌: shadows, glTF, PBR, skeletal animation, instancing, real WebGL shaders/framebuffers/`drawElements`, `webgpu` context — unsupported WebGL calls log `console.warn` and no-op (never crash) |\r\n| Dedicated Workers, Service Workers | 🟡/❌ | Dedicated `Worker` ✅: isolated `JsRuntime` per thread, `postMessage`/`onmessage`, binary/`structuredClone` payloads, error events, `terminate()`/`close()`, timers/console (data: `fetch` only), 16-msg/frame pump cap, 500 ms bounded shutdown. No `SharedArrayBuffer`, no DOM/window access, no nested workers, `transfer` is cloned. Service Workers ❌ |\r\n| XMLHttpRequest, IndexedDB, Notifications, Geolocation | ❌ | Not defined |\r\n| `<video>`/`<audio>` | ❌ | Not implemented |\r\n| Drag and drop | 🟡 | Native OS file drops deliver `dragenter`/`dragover`/`drop`/`dragleave` with a `DataTransfer` whose `files` carry `name` + Rendrix-extension `path` (read bytes only via `rendrix.fs` with permission). No draggable-element DnD, no `dragstart` synthesis from script yet |\r\n| `matchMedia` refinement | 🟡 | `prefers-reduced-motion` and `prefers-contrast` are answered on all native targets from `RENDRIX_REDUCED_MOTION=1` / `RENDRIX_CONTRAST_MORE=1`; real per-OS preference queries are not implemented on any platform yet |\r\n| `rendrix` module: `window`, `clipboard`, `quit`, `fs`, `dialog`, `shell`, `update` | ✅ | `fs` is limited to directories listed in `permissions.fs_read`/`fs_write`; `dialog`/`shell`/`update` documented below |\r\n\r\n## Measured performance (M0 harness)\r\n\r\nPipeline numbers live in [PERFORMANCE_AUDIT.md](PERFORMANCE_AUDIT.md) (the `bench 1000`\r\nscenarios plus the M0 per-scenario `shapes`/`restyles`/`layouts` counters). Node-side\r\nbuild costs, measured on this machine (Windows 11, RTX 3060) with\r\n`node packages/cli/bench/transpile.bench.mjs`:\r\n\r\n| Build step | Median |\r\n|---|---:|\r\n| `transpileModule`, one 1 KB TS file | 1.26 ms (200 iters) |\r\n| `buildApp`, 200-module project, no typecheck | 392.07 ms (5 iters) |\r\n| `buildApp`, 200-module project, with typecheck | 237.50 ms (3 iters, warm cache — run after the no-typecheck group) |\r\n\r\nMicro-benches (Criterion, dev-only, never shipped): `engine/crates/*/benches/`\r\n(`css`, `engine`, `taffy`, `text`, `js`, `pipeline`). Timing is informational in CI;\r\nallocation/shape-count deltas are asserted in `rendrix-runtime/tests/regression.rs`.\r\n\r\n## Conformance (WPT subset)\r\n\r\n[WPT.md](WPT.md) tracks a curated CSS layout subset (tables, floats, multi-column, plus\r\ngrid/flexbox regression guards) executed against the real headless runtime with\r\n`node scripts/wpt.mjs` (needs a built runtime). Pass rate is appended to\r\n`scripts/wpt-history.json` on every run and rendered into that page. It measures the\r\nsubset only — no browser parity is claimed, and it is not the full web-platform-tests suite.\r\n\r\n## Application platform\r\n\r\n| Capability | Status |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| Native window (winit), DPI scaling, resize, title, close | ✅ Windows x64 (manually verified); macOS/Linux built and tested in CI, not manually GPU-verified; Windows ARM64/x86 compile-checked, not run on hardware here |\r\n| Mouse, keyboard, wheel, text input, IME commit | ✅ Windows x64 (IME composition itself untested) |\r\n| System clipboard | ✅ via `arboard` (text) |\r\n| Single standalone executable (`rendrix package`) | ✅ Windows x64 (no external runtime; the bare `rendrix-runtime.exe` measured ~15–16 MB under the current release profile — see [PERF_BINARY_SIZE.md](PERF_BINARY_SIZE.md)); Windows ARM64/x86 packages plus macOS `.app` bundle and Linux binary layouts are wired in the CLI (compile-checked in CI, not run here) |\r\n| File dialogs, multi-window, tray, global shortcuts, auto-update, accessibility tree | 🟡/❌ | Dialogs, multi-window, the update client and the accessibility bridge are implemented (rows below); tray and global shortcuts remain ❌ |\r\n| Native file dialogs | ✅ | `rendrix.dialog.showOpenDialog({ title, filters: [{ name, extensions }], multiple, properties: ['openDirectory'] })` and `showSaveDialog({ title, defaultPath, filters })` → `Promise<string[] | null>`; OS UI runs on a worker thread (never blocks the frame loop); `Headless::set_dialog_mock` / `host.set_dialog_mock` for tests |\r\n| External links | ✅ | `rendrix.shell.openExternal(url)` — `http(s)`/`mailto:` only, fire-and-forget |\r\n| Multi-window | 🟡 | `window.open(url, target, 'width=W,height=H')` boots a real second window with an isolated `Session` (own engine + JS context); `handle.close()` / per-window close box drops it; last window out quits. No shared document/clipboard beyond the OS clipboard yet |\r\n| Accessibility tree | 🟡 | AccessKit bridge (`accesskit_winit`: UIA/NSAccessibility/AT-SPI) with role/name/state/bounds built from the DOM, AT actions (Click/Focus/Blur/SetValue/ReplaceSelectedText) routed to session entry points, updates pushed on repainted frames only; `prefers-reduced-motion`/`prefers-contrast` via `matchMedia` (environment-variable backed on all native targets). No manual Narrator/NVDA/VoiceOver/Orca pass yet — do not claim support (unexecuted procedure: [A11Y_CHECKLIST.md](A11Y_CHECKLIST.md)) |\r\n| App updates | 🟡 | `rendrix.update.check(feedUrl, version?)` → manifest `{ version, url, sha256 }`; `download(url, sha256)` verifies SHA-256 into a staged file; `install(path)` swaps the binary and relaunches (`quitAndInstall` semantics; Windows move-aside rename). Manifest written by `rendrix package --manifest` |\r\n| Code signing / installers | 🟡 | Helpers wired: `rendrix package --sign` (RENDRIX_SIGN_COMMAND / platform env), `--installer nsis` (Windows), `--manifest/--manifest-key/--publish-url`; macOS notarization helper present. No signed/macOS/Linux install runs yet |\r\n| Hot reload (`rendrix dev`) | ✅ | Rebuild diffs `bundle.modules`, writes `.rendrix/hot-update.json`; the running app picks it up via `RENDRIX_HOT_FILE` polling and hot-swaps modules in a fresh JS runtime on the live DOM (state preservation is script-cooperative; failed updates keep the last-good tree with the error logged). `--no-hot` restores restart behavior. End-to-end no-restart path verified at session level + CLI diff/sidecar tests |\r\n| Inspector | 🟡 | `rendrix-runtime --inspect out.json` (headless) dumps a JSON snapshot: DOM node table (capped at 500), computed styles, layout rects, `EngineStats` (incl. shaping signals), console tail, runtime errors. Snapshot on demand only, zero per-frame cost. No overlay UI |\r\n| Headless page render (`rendrix render page.html -o out.png` / `out.pdf` / `frames/`) | ✅ | PNG screenshot, one-page PDF, or a PNG frame sequence (the handoff the /video pipeline consumes; mp4 encoding is explicitly out of scope) through the existing headless path (`--screenshot` / `--pdf` / `--frame-dir`). Typechecking off; only the page plus the files it references are staged |\r\n| Solid adapter | ✅ | `packages/solid-adapter` (upstream `solid-js@1.9.19`, adapter-scoped dep) renders on the Rendrix DOM: mount/update/unmount/cleanup/events/`Show`/`For`/memo, `h` + `jsx-runtime` mapping, `onMount`/`onCleanup`, click handling. Headless 14-step matrix green. Limitations: `SVGElement` shim included; post-dispatch `currentTarget` cleanup warning is benign; `classList`-object-with-accessors is static (use function-valued props); `Show`/`For` need accessor props; no SSR/hydration; TSX `jsxImportSource` pragma unsupported (`buildApp` pins `rendrix`) |\r\n\r\n## Web target (wasm32-unknown-unknown, `rendrix-web`)\r\n\r\nThe same engine (CSS, DOM, layout, text, wgpu renderer, Web API prelude) compiled to WebAssembly.\r\nIt runs in a dedicated Worker (`engine/crates/rendrix-web`): the page owns the real `<canvas>` and the\r\nOS events and forwards them (`web/rendrix-web.js`); the worker runs the rAF loop (`web/rendrix-worker.js`)\r\nand reports back what the page must do (cursor, soft keyboard, title, clipboard writes, external links).\r\n`cargo check --target wasm32-unknown-unknown` passes for\r\n`rendrix-css/-dom/-layout/-core/-gfx/-js`, `rendrix-runtime` (lib + the native-only CLI, which is a\r\nwasm stub) and `rendrix-web`. Native-only code in `rendrix-js/src/host.rs` (`std::thread` fetch,\r\n`rfd` dialogs, shell `Command`, the updater, `tungstenite`, worker threads) and the QuickJS backend\r\n(`rquickjs`) are gated `not(wasm32)`; timers use `web_time::Instant` (`std::time::Instant` panics on wasm).\r\n\r\n| Capability | Status | Notes |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| JavaScript engine | 🟡 | The browser's own engine, not QuickJS: `BrowserEngine` (`rendrix-web/src/engine.rs`) routes `__native(op, ...args)` to the same `DomHost`, runs the same prelude, and forwards console output to the page. No bundling of an engine in the wasm binary; browser JIT performance |\r\n| ES modules | 🟡 | Each bundle module becomes a Blob URL with static specifiers rewritten post-order to dependency URLs, so the browser loader does linking, TLA and live bindings. Literal and computed `import()` go through `__rendrix_dynImport`, resolved against the bundle map at call time; unknown specifiers reject. **Static import cycles cannot be expressed with Blob URLs and are reported as errors** — keep the module graph acyclic for the web target. `boot` (`DOMContentLoaded`/`load`) is deferred until the module queue is idle, as in a page |\r\n| Tasks and microtasks | 🟡 | Microtasks cannot be drained on demand (`run_jobs` is a no-op; promise jobs run when control returns to the worker event loop). The frame loop still settles several extra frames after input so queued jobs land. **No execution-budget interrupt**: a runaway script hangs the worker (the page stays alive), whereas native QuickJS is preempted after 5 s/task |\r\n| Rendering | 🟡 | wgpu `BROWSER_WEBGPU \\| GL` on the transferred `OffscreenCanvas`, with downlevel WebGL2 limits requested where WebGPU is missing. Instance creation probes for a *usable* WebGPU adapter (`new_instance_with_webgpu_detection`): a bare `Instance::new` locks onto the WebGPU-only path from `navigator.gpu` alone, which headless Chromium (SwiftShader) exposes without being able to create an adapter. A manually reported headless Chromium 153 run was green (10 checks: mount, rAF frames, in-app clicks, storage, dialog rejection, WS error event) with SwiftShader WebGPU flags (`--enable-unsafe-swiftshader --in-process-gpu --disable-gpu-sandbox`); no automated browser driver test is checked into this repository, and real-GPU runs are untested. When the device has no storage buffers, the renderer now uses a uniform-backed 48-instance array with chunked draws and a uniform polygon buffer instead of SSBOs; a native pixel test under `downlevel_webgl2_defaults()` is identical to the WebGPU path, and the native single-storage-buffer path is unchanged. A real no-WebGPU browser run is still unrecorded, so treat this target as unverified on such browsers |\r\n| Input and environment | ✅ | Pointer/touch/wheel, keys, IME composition, text commit, paste, resize/DPR, focus, safe area, keyboard height, `prefers-color-scheme`, `maxTouchPoints`, gamepads (polled on the page — the Gamepad API is main-thread only) are forwarded by `rendrix-web.js`. `WebApp::eval` evaluates expressions in the app for diagnostics/tests |\r\n| `fetch` | ✅ | Browser `fetch` behind the host HTTP hook (forbidden headers are dropped by the browser); `data:` and bundle-relative URLs as on native |\r\n| Clipboard | 🟡 | App copies are forwarded to `navigator.clipboard`; pastes arrive as page events. No `clipboardchange` events |\r\n| `localStorage`/`sessionStorage` | 🟡 | In-memory only on the web target; nothing is persisted to browser `localStorage` yet (hook is follow-up work) |\r\n| `rendrix.fs` | ❌ | No filesystem on the web target: every op fails with the permission error |\r\n| `rendrix.dialog` | 🟡 | Rejects actionably (`file dialogs are not available on the web target (use an <input type=file> element instead)`) instead of pretending the user cancelled |\r\n| `rendrix.shell.openExternal` | ✅ | Forwarded to the page, which opens `http(s)`/`mailto:` in a new tab (`noopener,noreferrer`) |\r\n| `WebSocket` | ❌ | The socket handshake needs an OS thread per connection: script gets an `error` event (`WebSocket is not available on the web target yet`). Browser-backed sockets are follow-up work |\r\n| Dedicated Workers | ❌ | Spawning answers `error` + `close` (`Workers are not supported on the web target yet`); the main-thread `Worker` class still exists for feature detection. Browser-Worker backing is follow-up work |\r\n| `rendrix.update` | ❌ | Rejects actionably (`app updates do not apply to the web target`) |\r\n| `matchMedia` refinement | 🟡 | `prefers-color-scheme` follows the page; `prefers-reduced-motion`/`prefers-contrast` still read the (absent on wasm) env overrides — pushing the browser settings through is follow-up work |\r\n\r\n## Mobile entry scaffolding (follow-up — no NDK/mac toolchain in this environment)\r\n\r\n`Session` is platform-independent: touch (tap/pan/fling/long-press/multi-touch/`touch-action`), safe-area\r\nand keyboard insets as `env()`, soft-keyboard intent and gamepads are driven through its public entry points\r\nand covered by `engine/crates/rendrix-runtime/tests/mobile.rs`, which runs on a desktop with no device or\r\nemulator. The OS shells that would drive `Session` on phones do not exist yet:\r\n\r\n- Android: `rendrix-runtime/src/lib.rs` declares a `#[cfg(target_os = \"android\")] pub mod android;`\r\n  whose file is not present — the NDK shell (activity entry, `Session` driver, APK asset loading,\r\n  memory clipboard, gamepad routing) is unwritten. Nothing has been built for Android.\r\n- iOS: no Swift/ObjC shell (wgpu Metal surface + `Session` driver) exists. Nothing has been built for iOS.\r\n- The desktop-only backends already exclude these targets by cfg (`arboard`/`gilrs` are\r\n  `not(any(android, ios, wasm32))`; `Session` takes any `Clipboard`, e.g. the in-tree memory one), so the\r\n  shells above only need to supply platform plumbing, not engine changes.\r\n",
  "docs/BUILDING.md": "# Building and running\r\n\r\n## Requirements\r\n\r\n* Rust (stable) and a C/C++ toolchain: MSVC Build Tools on Windows, Xcode command line tools on macOS,\r\n  `build-essential` plus X11/Wayland development headers on Linux.\r\n* Node.js 18+ (the CLI and the TypeScript compiler). Bun or npm both work for installing.\r\n* A GPU with a Vulkan, Metal or DirectX 12 driver. The runtime picks the adapter itself;\r\n  `rendrix doctor` prints which one.\r\n\r\nOnly Windows x64 has been manually exercised with GPU-visible output (see\r\n[COMPATIBILITY.md](COMPATIBILITY.md)). macOS and Linux are built and tested in CI, but no manual run has\r\nbeen recorded. Windows ARM64 and x86 are compile-checked in CI and cross-packaged by tests, but have not\r\nbeen run on hardware here.\r\n\r\n## Build the runtime\r\n\r\n```sh\r\ncd engine\r\ncargo test --workspace                      # 410 Rust tests / 2 ignored in the 2026-11-24 run (GPU tests skip with no adapter)\r\ncargo build --release -p rendrix-runtime    # engine/target/release/rendrix-runtime[.exe]\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe CLI finds the runtime through `RENDRIX_RUNTIME`, then `engine/target/{release,debug}`, then\r\n`$RENDRIX_HOME/runtime/<platform>-<arch>/`.\r\n\r\n## Create and run an application\r\n\r\n```sh\r\nnpm install                                  # once, at the repository root (installs TypeScript)\r\nnode packages/cli/bin/rendrix.mjs init my-app\r\ncd my-app\r\nrendrix dev        # builds, opens a native window, hot-reloads changed modules on the live DOM\r\nrendrix build      # type-check + compile to dist/my-app.rdxapp\r\nrendrix run        # build and run once\r\nrendrix check      # type-check only\r\nrendrix package    # dist/my-app.exe: one standalone executable, no Node/Bun/browser needed\r\nrendrix render     # headless page → PNG, PDF or a PNG frame sequence\r\nrendrix doctor     # Node, TypeScript, runtime, GPU adapter, project config\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Cross-target packaging\r\n\r\nPackaging is target-driven, not host-driven:\r\n\r\n```sh\r\nrendrix package --target x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu --runtime ./runtimes/linux-x64/rendrix-runtime\r\nrendrix package --target aarch64-apple-darwin --runtime ./runtimes/darwin-arm64/rendrix-runtime\r\nrendrix package --target i686-pc-windows-msvc --runtime ./runtimes/win32-x86/rendrix-runtime.exe  # 32-bit Windows\r\nrendrix package --target armv7-unknown-linux-gnueabihf --runtime ./runtimes/linux-armv7/rendrix-runtime  # Raspberry Pi (32-bit)\r\n```\r\n\r\nSupported target keys are `win32-x64`, `win32-arm64`, `win32-x86`, `darwin-x64`, `darwin-arm64`,\r\n`linux-x64`, `linux-x86`, `linux-arm64`, `linux-armv7` and `linux-riscv64` (Rust triples and short\r\naliases such as `macos-intel` also work). Windows x86 is the 32-bit target:\r\n`i686-pc-windows-msvc` / `i686-pc-windows-gnu` (aliases `x86` / `ia32`) map to the `win32-x86` key,\r\nalongside `win32-x64` and `win32-arm64`. Linux adds three packaging targets beyond x64/arm64: 32-bit\r\nx86 (`i686-unknown-linux-gnu`), 32-bit ARM (`armv7-unknown-linux-gnueabihf`, aliases `armv7` /\r\n`armhf`, the Raspberry Pi 32-bit target) and 64-bit RISC-V (`riscv64gc-unknown-linux-gnu`, alias\r\n`riscv64`); Node on a 32-bit ARM Linux host reports arch `arm`, which the CLI detects as\r\n`linux-armv7`. A cross-target build never picks up a local `engine/target` runtime, because that\r\nbinary is host-only — pass `--runtime` or place binaries under\r\n`$RENDRIX_HOME/runtime/<platform>-<arch>/`.\r\n\r\nBuilding the engine for `i686-pc-windows-msvc` needs **libclang (LLVM)** on the build machine: `rquickjs-sys`\r\nships no pregenerated bindings for that triple, so the `bindgen` feature is enabled automatically for 32-bit\r\nWindows. Set `LIBCLANG_PATH` if libclang is not on the default search path.\r\n\r\nCross-compiling the engine for the extra Linux architectures needs the matching cross C toolchain, because\r\n`rquickjs` (QuickJS) and `ring` compile C code for the target; `rquickjs-sys` 0.14 does ship pregenerated\r\nbindings for all three triples, so no libclang step is involved. On Debian/Ubuntu:\r\n\r\n```sh\r\nsudo apt-get install gcc-arm-linux-gnueabihf libudev-dev  # or gcc-i686-linux-gnu / gcc-riscv64-linux-gnu\r\nexport CC_armv7_unknown_linux_gnueabihf=arm-linux-gnueabihf-gcc\r\nexport CARGO_TARGET_ARMV7_UNKNOWN_LINUX_GNUEABIHF_LINKER=arm-linux-gnueabihf-gcc\r\nexport PKG_CONFIG_ALLOW_CROSS=1                          # gilrs' libudev-sys build script probes pkg-config\r\ncargo check --target armv7-unknown-linux-gnueabihf -p rendrix-runtime --manifest-path engine/Cargo.toml\r\n```\r\n\r\n`cargo check` runs build scripts but never links, so the host's pkg-config metadata satisfies libudev.\r\nOn a Windows or macOS host there is no practical way to install the Linux cross C compilers, so those\r\nchecks are owned by the `linux-cross-compile` CI job (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`).\r\n\r\nmacOS produces `<name>.app/Contents/{MacOS,Resources,Info.plist,PkgInfo}` and a zipped `.app` for\r\ndistribution; `--sign` signs the bundle and the notarization step submits the zip and staples the app.\r\nLinux produces a `.tar.gz` with `bin/`, a freedesktop `.desktop` entry and a hicolor icon. Pass a square\r\n`--icon <file>` (`.png` or `.icns`) to override the generated default icon on either platform. NSIS\r\ninstallers remain Windows-only.\r\n\r\nA project is `rendrix.json` (name, window size/title, permissions), an `index.html` (with `<link\r\nrel=\"stylesheet\">` and `<script type=\"module\" src=\"…ts|tsx\">`), `src/**`, and any assets. `tsconfig.json`\r\nselects `\"jsx\": \"react-jsx\"` and `\"jsxImportSource\": \"rendrix\"`.\r\n\r\n`rendrix dev` rebuilds and hot-swaps changed modules into a fresh JS runtime on the **live DOM**. State\r\npreservation is script-cooperative: globals and DOM state survive when the script re-initialises them, and a\r\nfailed update keeps the last-good tree with the error logged. Use `--no-hot` to restore restart-on-change.\r\nThe optional `--inspect out.json` runtime flag dumps a DOM/style/layout/engine-stats snapshot; there is no\r\noverlay inspector UI yet.\r\n\r\n## Verifying a build\r\n\r\n```sh\r\nnpm test                 # cargo test --workspace + the CLI test suite (runs bundles in the real runtime)\r\nnpm run e2e              # builds examples/app-counter, replays scripted clicks/resizes headlessly on the GPU,\r\n                         # fails if any expectation breaks, writes screenshots to .rendrix-shots/\r\nnpm run wpt              # curated CSS layout conformance subset against the headless runtime\r\nnpm run bench            # frame-pipeline timings on a 1,000-item list (release build)\r\n\r\n# Headless rendering of a standalone page (no project needed):\r\nrendrix render page.html -o out.png        # also out.pdf, or frames/ for a PNG sequence\r\n# Optional experimental wasm target (needs wasm32-unknown-unknown + wasm-bindgen-cli):\r\ncargo check --target wasm32-unknown-unknown --manifest-path engine/Cargo.toml -p rendrix-web\r\n```\r\n\r\nRuntime flags useful for debugging: `--headless --screenshot out.png`, `--script steps.json`\r\n(steps: `click`, `move`, `type`, `key`, `wheel`, `resize`, `wait`, `settle`, `eval`, `expect`, `screenshot`),\r\n`--size WxH`, `--scale S`. Environment: `RENDRIX_DUMP_FRAME=file.png` writes the frame the window presents,\r\n`RENDRIX_TRACE_EVENTS=1` logs window events.\r\n\r\n## Reproducibility\r\n\r\n`engine/Cargo.lock` is committed; Rust dependencies resolve from it. The JavaScript side uses the\r\nTypeScript compiler version from `package.json`. Release profile: fat LTO, one codegen\r\nunit per crate, stripped symbols, `opt-level = 3`; see [PERF_BINARY_SIZE.md](PERF_BINARY_SIZE.md).\r\nDev/test builds are unchanged.\r\n",
  "docs/SAFETY.md": "# Safety and permissions\r\n\r\n**Rendrix runs your application's code with the privileges of the user who starts it, plus a small set of\r\ncapability checks. It is not a sandbox for hostile code.** Only run applications you trust.\r\n\r\n## What is enforced\r\n\r\n| Capability | Default | How it is enforced |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| Network (`fetch` to `http(s)`) | **denied** | `permissions.network` in `rendrix.json`; otherwise `fetch` rejects with a `TypeError`. There is no per-host allow-list for `fetch`. WebSocket has one hardcoded exception: loopback (`localhost`, `127.0.0.1`, `::1`) is always allowed, even when `permissions.network` is false. |\r\n| File reads | **denied** | Only through `rendrix.fs`; paths are canonicalised and must lie inside a directory listed in `permissions.fs_read`. Plain Web APIs cannot touch the filesystem. |\r\n| File writes | **denied** | Same, with `permissions.fs_write`. |\r\n| Relative `fetch`, images, fonts, stylesheets | bundled assets only | `DirAssets` and bundle assets reject `..` segments. |\r\n| General process spawning, native add-ons, Node/Bun APIs | **do not exist** | There is no general script-facing spawn/add-on API. Two narrow host operations do reach the OS: `rendrix.update.install(path)` re-launches the current executable via `std::process::Command::spawn()`, and `rendrix.shell.openExternal()` asks the OS to open a URL. Neither accepts an arbitrary command. |\r\n| Remote script/module loading | **do not exist** | The build refuses `http(s):`/`node:` imports; the module loader only reads the bundle. |\r\n\r\nCovered by tests: `filesystem_access_is_permission_gated` (reads, writes, denied paths, denied network),\r\nbundle trailer/format validation, and build-time rejection of Node built-ins and CommonJS.\r\n\r\n## What is not enforced\r\n\r\n* The execution budget is a liveness guard, not a sandbox: native QuickJS interrupts a task after 5 s and\r\n  reports it as an error, and memory is capped at 1 GiB with a 2 MiB stack. Workers are separate JS\r\n  contexts but run in the same process. On the experimental wasm target there is no execution-budget\r\n  interrupt, so a runaway script hangs the worker (the page stays alive).\r\n* QuickJS and native crates are not hardened against malicious inputs; treat untrusted images, fonts and\r\n  HTML as a risk.\r\n* Scripts can read the whole bundle and their own `localStorage` (a plain JSON file in the user data\r\n  directory, in-memory only on the web target). Nothing is encrypted.\r\n* A bundle appended to an executable is not integrity-checked by the runtime. Signing helpers are wired\r\n  (`rendrix package --sign`, `--manifest`, `--manifest-key`, `--publish-url`, `--installer nsis`), but\r\n  packages are unsigned by default and no signed macOS/Linux install has been run or recorded.\r\n* `crypto.getRandomValues` uses the OS CSPRNG. `crypto.subtle.digest` (SHA-1/256/384/512) is available; the rest of `SubtleCrypto` does not exist.\r\n\r\n## Reporting\r\n\r\nOpen a private security advisory on the repository. Please include the bundle or script that reproduces\r\nthe behaviour.\r\n"
};
